// trap: .on_delete(cascade) keeps its one-row delete, with no guard and no DanglingKey rule.
// The lifecycle does not run a cascade yet: CancelDraft deletes the Order and no line, and
// no guard waits for the lines, since the database would remove them. CancelDraft marks the
// line it binds, which the Order's key names, as orphaned in the same step, so the line is
// left present and orphaned after Open, AddLine, CancelDraft, and Forbidden_OrderLine_0
// fails. The key gets no DanglingKey_* rule: the engine does not run the cascade, so a
// counterexample there would describe the engine, not the model. The info
// DeleteLeavesChildren names the use case. An engine that put the restrict guard on a
// cascade key would never run CancelDraft while the line names the Order and would answer
// ok. z3 meets the same step from a state where the rule holds, so the rule is unproved.
// expect Forbidden_OrderLine_0: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample z3=unproved
entity Order "注文" { id: Int @pk }
entity OrderLine "明細" { id: Int @pk  orphaned: Bool @default(false) }
relate(OrderLine, Order, N:1).on_delete(cascade)
usecase Open "起票"
usecase AddLine "明細追加"
usecase CancelDraft "下書き取消"
creates(Open, Order)
creates(AddLine, OrderLine)
deletes(CancelDraft, Order)
sets(CancelDraft, OrderLine.orphaned == true)
forbidden(OrderLine, OrderLine.orphaned == true)
